        "text": "# Creative Collation Scan: GLP-1 Women talk\n\n> ⚠️ Image-only creative: hook and copy framing use only available title/body/transcript metadata; no OCR or visual extraction was performed.\n\n## Scan scope\n\nCreative collation: 1513272747503535\nRepresentative ad: facebook_3291016807753829\nActive ads: 1 / 2\nMember ad IDs: facebook_1519895792794446, facebook_3291016807753829\n\n## 1. Hook / opening creative text\n\n> How I finally beat my Mounjaro side effects\n\nSource: Primary ad text lead fallback; not visual/OCR extraction.\nPattern: unclassified.\nPattern reason: No supported hook-pattern heuristic matched the hook text.\n\n## 2. Copy framing\n\nHow I finally beat my Mounjaro side effects\n\nFour months in, and for the first three of them I felt worse than I expected to, if I'm honest. The weight was coming off, which was the whole point, but I was constipated more days than not, nauseous most mornings, and so foggy by early afternoon I couldn't hold a proper conversation. Nobody prepares you for that part. You see the number on the scale and assume everything else is just noise you push through.\n\nI pushed through for way longer than I should have. Tried a probiotic on its own, didn't touch the fog or the energy. Tried a multivitamin, made the nausea worse if I took it without eating properly, which on the jabs is most days.\n\nWhat actually turned it around was Cloud. Three gummies, once a day, no tablets to choke down on a bad stomach morning. They have 36 superfood ingredients designed specifically for people on the jabs. Live probiotics and plant fibre for the constipation and bloating, B12, folate and lion's mane for the fog, the full spread of what a suppressed appetite quietly stops giving you enough of.\n\nWithin the first couple of weeks the constipation had properly eased. The nausea followed not long after. And the brain fog - that was the one I didn't expect to lift, but by week four I was feeling clear as day, and so much more in control of my mind.\n\nI’m still on the jab, still losing weight, but I’m actually feeling like myself while it happens instead of just tolerating it to get to the number on the scale.\n\nI can assure you, you won't regret trying it. And there's a 60 day money back guarantee anyway, so there's no reason to not try it.\n\n→ Cloud. 3 gummies a day.\n\nThe Better Way to Support Your Body\n\n## 3. Creative structure\n\nFormat: **image**\nCTA: **LEARN MORE** — Free Shipping on Subscription\nMedia URL: https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/c0823460e8748f1a0c709a7af10208354c8f6566b66074c1552e802e57006c60.jpg\n\n## 4. Landing page\n\nhttps://usecloud.co/pages/glp-1-v20#CTA _(domain: usecloud.co)_\n\n## 5. Performance signals\n\nReach: 81,531\nEstimated spend: €734\nAdvertiser reach (30d): 218,996\nLaunched: 2026-07-15\nStill live: Yes (54 days running)\nRank trajectory: improving\n\n## 6. Verdict\n\n**Scaling hard — worth modeling.**\n\n---\nCredits used: 3 | Remaining: 8462 | Source: recurring\nBreakdown: ad_detail:1(success), reach_history:1(success)"
